.TH ACC-CATALOG 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-catalog \- serve a writable ACC package catalog over HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-catalog
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-catalog
is a package catalog that
.BR acc-pkg (1)
can install from and publish to.
It serves \fIindex.json\fR and the package files to the resolver, and
accepts uploads from \fBacc\-pkg publish\fR.
.PP
An upload is staged until its signature arrives, then verified, and only a
verified package is promoted into the index.
A package whose signature does not verify, or that an Enterprise Contract
policy rejects, is refused and logged.
Writes need a bearer token; with no token configured uploads are disabled
and the catalog is read-only.
.PP
The command takes no arguments; it is configured through the environment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_ROOT
The data directory (default \fI/var/lib/acc\-catalog\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_TIER
The tier tag written into the index (default \fBcommunity\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_PUBKEY
A cosign public key (PEM); when set, packages are verified in keypair mode.
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_SIGNER_ISSUER
The OIDC issuer for keyless verification, or an audit label in keypair
mode (default \fBlab\-keypair\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_SIGNER_SUBJECT
The subject regular expression for keyless verification (default \fB.*\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_EC_POLICY
An Enterprise Contract policy file (default: an empty policy).
.TP
.B ACC_CATALOG_TOKEN
The bearer token uploads must carry.
Unset disables uploads; reads are still served.
.TP
.BR ACC_CATALOG_HOST ", " ACC_CATALOG_PORT
The bind address (default \fB0.0.0.0\fR, meant to sit behind an ingress)
and port (default \fB8080\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/acc\-catalog
Staged uploads, promoted packages and the index.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ACC_CATALOG_ROOT=/srv/catalog ACC_CATALOG_PUBKEY=/etc/acc/cosign.pub \e
  ACC_CATALOG_TOKEN=... acc\-catalog
acc\-pkg publish dist/my_role.accpkg \-\-catalog\-url http://localhost:8080/
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc-pkg (1),
.BR acc (1),
.BR cosign (1)
